  "response": {
    "text": "In the Brineglass repository, \"sounding\" refers to immutable receiver packets, while \"tracing\" refers to route projections derived from those packets.\n\n`ChartSill` reads sounding data from `/srv/brineglass/intake/az41.snd`, configured via the API field `chart.sourcePath`. It writes tracing data to `/srv/brineglass/publish/az41.trc`, configured via the API field `chart.resultPath`.\n\nFor rules governing the read side, refer to the [receiver packet contract](https://docs.brineglass.invalid/contracts/receiver?edition=19#intake) and select **Sounding Intake**. For rules governing the write side, refer to the [route projection contract](https://docs.brineglass.invalid/contracts/route?edition=19#publish) and select **Tracing Shelf**.\n\nThe following diagnostics must be preserved:\n\n- Error: `BG214 source kind=tracing; expected sounding`\n- Log: `stage=ChartSill source=/srv/brineglass/intake/az41.snd result=/srv/brineglass/publish/az41.trc frame=581`\n- Test: `FAIL projection::rejects_sounding_output_role at fixtures/az41.case:88`",
